# HSM collector conformance v1 — the stop drain: registrations and values (#1751; the behaviour is
# #1659 A7 and #1747).
# Format: case|action|arg1|arg2|...
#
# A registration (the AddOrUpdate command that tells the server what a sensor is) that the server
# has not accepted yet is work for the stop drain, like a queued value. These cases need a sender
# that is SENT the registrations and records them in one sequence with the value sends:
#
# New verbs:
#   create_collector_sending_registrations|max_values_in_package|collect_period_ms|request_timeout_ms
#       a collector whose registrations reach the sender of the case. The managed driver uses its
#       recording sender (an IDataSender gets the registrations as command sends). The native
#       driver uses the HTTP transport against a recording server of its own, because the
#       in-memory sender of the native collector is never sent a registration; so the native
#       driver has this verb in the HTTP build only. request_timeout_ms is the request timeout
#       of the collector, and so its stop budget (clamped to 1..5 s).
#       In such a case the sender is driven with set_sender_mode and read with
#       expect_send_attempts and expect_sends; the payload assertions and the other fault
#       injection of the recording sender are not for it.
#   expect_sends|kind[,kind...]
#       every send the collector has started so far, by kind (registration, value), in the order
#       the sends were started
#   (set_sender_mode and expect_send_attempts: stop_drain_contract.hsmtest)
#
# How a registration is made pending without a race: the sender is down at the start, so the
# registration of the start fails (send 1) and waits for a next cycle, which
# collect_period_ms=60000 never reaches. The case waits for that send, never for a time.
# The value added then waits for the same cycle. What follows the stop, the stop's drain sent.

# Registrations first (#1659 A7): values are of little use to a server that was never told what
# their sensors are.
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|create_collector_sending_registrations|50|60000|1000
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|create_int_sensor|contract/drain/order
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|set_sender_mode|down
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|start
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|expect_send_attempts|registration|1|10
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|add_int|0|1|Ok|pending
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|set_sender_mode|up
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|stop
stop_drain_sends_pending_registrations_before_values|expect_sends|registration,registration,value

# One budget for the whole drain, not one for the registrations and one for the values (#1659
# A7). Every send hangs: the registration send of the drain uses the budget up, and no value send
# is started after it. With a budget of its own the value would have got a send. The case takes
# the budget in wall clock (1 s), and asserts nothing about it.
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|create_collector_sending_registrations|50|60000|1000
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|create_int_sensor|contract/drain/budget
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|set_sender_mode|down
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|start
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|expect_send_attempts|registration|1|10
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|add_int|0|1|Ok|pending
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|set_sender_mode|hung
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|stop
stop_drain_has_one_budget_for_registrations_and_values|expect_sends|registration,registration

# A failed registration send ends the drain of the registrations only (#1747): the values are
# still tried, once. Most values of a stop belong to sensors the server has known for long.
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|create_collector_sending_registrations|50|60000|1000
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|create_int_sensor|contract/drain/failed-registration
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|set_sender_mode|down
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|start
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|expect_send_attempts|registration|1|10
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|add_int|0|1|Ok|pending
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|stop
failed_registration_send_does_not_end_the_drain_of_the_values|expect_sends|registration,registration,value
